<FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" VerticalGap="16px" Class="my-2">
    <FluentText>
        The Training system lets Managers and Admins build courses, assign them to staff, and
        track who has completed what. This page covers the pieces that make it up and how they
        fit together.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Key terms</FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Course</strong>, the top-level unit of training. Has a name, description,
            pass mark, and belongs to a location.</li>
        <li><strong>Section</strong>, a block of reading content inside a course. A course can
            have several, shown to the trainee in order.</li>
        <li><strong>Quiz question</strong>, a multiple-choice question attached to a course, with
            one correct option. All of a course's questions make up its single quiz.</li>
        <li><strong>Assignment</strong>, links one course to one staff member. This is what
            actually shows up in someone's "My Training" list, and what carries the due date and
            completion status.</li>
        <li><strong>Recurrence</strong>, an optional setting on a course that automatically
            re-assigns it to someone a set number of months after they last completed it (a
            "retake").</li>
    </ul>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Assignment status</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Every assignment is always in exactly one of these states, worked out automatically,
        there's nothing to set manually:
    </FluentText>
    <FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" VerticalGap="8px">
        <FluentStack VerticalAlignment="VerticalAlignment.Center" HorizontalGap="12px">
            <FluentBadge Content="Not Started" Color="BadgeColor.Subtle" Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" />
            <FluentText>The person hasn't opened the course yet.</FluentText>
        </FluentStack>
        <FluentStack VerticalAlignment="VerticalAlignment.Center" HorizontalGap="12px">
            <FluentBadge Content="In Progress" Color="BadgeColor.Informative" Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" />
            <FluentText>They've started at least one section but haven't finished.</FluentText>
        </FluentStack>
        <FluentStack VerticalAlignment="VerticalAlignment.Center" HorizontalGap="12px">
            <FluentBadge Content="Completed" Color="BadgeColor.Success" Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" />
            <FluentText>They've finished and, if there's a quiz, passed it.</FluentText>
        </FluentStack>
        <FluentStack VerticalAlignment="VerticalAlignment.Center" HorizontalGap="12px">
            <FluentBadge Content="Overdue" Color="BadgeColor.Danger" Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" />
            <FluentText>The due date has passed and it still isn't completed.</FluentText>
        </FluentStack>
    </FluentStack>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Manager vs Admin</FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Managers</strong> can create/edit courses for their own location, assign
            training to individuals or by role, and view reports for their location.</li>
        <li><strong>Admins</strong> can do everything a Manager can, plus: change which location a
            course belongs to, and manage courses/assignments across every location.</li>
    </ul>
    <FluentText>
        See the <strong>Multi-Location Training Rules</strong> tab for more on how location
        ownership and sharing works.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Where to find things</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        The <a href="/manage/training">Training Dashboard</a> has five tabs: <strong>By
        Course</strong> and <strong>By Person</strong> for viewing and managing assignments,
        <strong>Auto-assign rules</strong> for new-user defaults, and <strong>Timing</strong> /
        <strong>Analytics</strong> for reports. Courses themselves are created and edited from the
        separate <a href="/manage/training/courses">Courses</a> page.
    </FluentText>
</FluentStack>
